{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-k2-reviewer-fable-50","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:2c458d2b523ea8c1bd90","verdict":"demonstrated_issue","issue_class":"issue-class:repeated-authorized-independent-unit-entry-into-row-independent-procedure","bounded_statement":"Within the supplied files for case:2c458d2b523ea8c1bd90, the selected result runs an exact two-sided binomial sign test that enters all 20 recording windows as independent trials, even though the data description designates gearbox_id as the independent unit and the 20 windows come from only 6 gearboxes (each gearbox contributing up to 4 rows). The reported rejection of the 50% null (15/20 wins, p = 0.0414) therefore relies on repeated entries of the same independent unit into a row-independent procedure, and the stated conclusion is not supported at the declared unit of independence by the provided workflow.","root_cause":"The workflow (workflow/analysis.py) computes n_lower and n_windows over raw CSV rows and calls binomtest(n_lower, n_windows, 0.5) without any aggregation, deduplication, or clustering adjustment by gearbox_id. Because windows from the same gearbox share machine-level acoustic characteristics and are declared non-independent by the data description, the effective sample size is at most 6 independent units, not 20, so the binomial trial-count and the resulting p-value of 0.0414 overstate the evidence; the significance claim at alpha = 0.05 is derived from an inflated trial count.","evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The data description designates gearbox_id as the independent-unit column and states that gearboxes repeat across rows.","observed_value":"Independent unit column: gearbox_id; same gearbox contributes several windows","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":11,"end_line":11,"quoted_text":"Independent unit column: gearbox_id"},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":16,"end_line":17,"quoted_text":"- `gearbox_id` - identifier of the gearbox the window came from. The same\n  gearbox contributed several windows, so this value repeats across rows."},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":23,"end_line":24,"quoted_text":"The table holds 20 windows drawn from 6 gearboxes, so the windows are clustered\nwithin a much smaller number of machines."}]},{"description":"The input data shows repeated gearbox_id values; e.g., gearbox G-14 alone contributes four rows, confirming multiple entries per independent unit.","observed_value":"G-14 appears in 4 rows; 6 distinct gearbox_id values across 20 rows","source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":2,"end_line":5,"quoted_text":"G-14,W-1401,low,64.8,62.3\nG-14,W-1402,low,65.2,63.9\nG-14,W-1403,mid,67.1,68.0\nG-14,W-1404,mid,66.4,64.7"}]},{"description":"The workflow counts wins over all rows and passes the row count as the binomial trial count with no grouping by gearbox_id anywhere in the script.","observed_value":"binomtest(n_lower=15, n_windows=20, 0.5) computed over raw rows","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":33,"end_line":37,"quoted_text":"    reductions = [reduction_db(w) for w in windows]\n    n_windows = len(reductions)\n    n_lower = sum(1 for value in reductions if value > 0.0)\n    share = n_lower / n_windows\n    outcome = binomtest(n_lower, n_windows, NULL_SHARE, alternative=\"two-sided\")"}]},{"description":"The report's selected result explicitly claims the 20 windows were entered as independent trials and rejects the null at alpha = 0.05 on that basis.","observed_value":"15/20 wins, p = 0.0414, null rejected at alpha = 0.05","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":28,"end_line":28,"quoted_text":"[selected-result] Exact two-sided binomial sign test over 20 recording windows entered as independent trials: the adaptive gate reached the lower noise floor in 15 of 20 windows (share 0.750, median reduction 1.40 dB), p = 0.0414, so the 50% null is rejected at alpha = 0.05."},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":16,"end_line":19,"quoted_text":"the lower floor. Every window in the table was entered as one\nindependent trial in an exact two-sided binomial sign test\n(`scipy.stats.binomtest`) against the null hypothesis that the adaptive\ngate wins in half of the windows."}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"The report transparently discloses that only 6 gearboxes are represented among the 20 windows, so the clustering is not concealed; a reader could in principle discount the claim. This does not, however, change the fact that the test itself treats the 20 rows as independent trials.","observed_value":"Gearboxes represented: 6","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":6,"end_line":7,"quoted_text":"- Recording windows analysed: 20\n- Gearboxes represented: 6"}]},{"description":"The data description also states 'One trial is: one row', which the authors could cite as authorization for row-level trials; but the same description names gearbox_id as the independent unit and stresses clustering, so row-level trials still violate the binomial test's independence requirement.","observed_value":"One trial is: one row","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":12,"end_line":12,"quoted_text":"One trial is: one row"},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":11,"end_line":11,"quoted_text":"Independent unit column: gearbox_id"}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I tried to falsify the finding three ways. (1) I checked whether each gearbox in data/input.csv contributes only one row, which would make rows coincide with independent units; instead G-14 and G-33 contribute 4 rows each and G-21, G-47, G-52, G-68 contribute 3 each, so 6 units span 20 rows. (2) I searched workflow/analysis.py for any aggregation, per-gearbox summarization, or cluster-robust adjustment before binomtest; none exists — gearbox_id is only used to count distinct machines for the report header. (3) I recomputed the analysis from the raw data: per-row reductions yield 15 positives of 20 and an exact two-sided binomial p of about 0.0414, matching the report, confirming the p-value indeed comes from the row-level trial count of 20 rather than the 6 independent units. A per-gearbox aggregation (e.g., majority sign per gearbox gives 6 of 6 favoring the adaptive gate, exact two-sided p = 0.03125) is a different procedure not performed by the workflow, so it cannot rescue the stated 20-trial result. All checks confirm rather than refute the issue.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]}